{"id":"ai-terminal-ysr","content_hash":"57f098ec3e53201cae7e554f83e2f9ad1183991171b39404a602c79d4dbbe6c0","title":"Decouple fencing/truncation from REPL","description":"Context: Agent B currently emits raw stdout in final messages (e.g., cycle 5aaef586), and the REPL adds fences/truncation based on output_value_types. This means the REPL is adding content instead of just presenting. Problem: REPL should be a dumb presenter; fencing/truncation and block decisions should come from orchestrator/agents. We need to design an upstream contract where Agent B/orchestrator provide explicit segments/placeholders with tags and any truncation instructions, leaving REPL to render faithfully. Status: Solution open; needs upstream contract/prompt redesign and UI changes aligned with spec v1.5.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-11-20T15:41:54.811125881-05:00","updated_at":"2025-11-20T15:41:54.811125881-05:00","source_repo":".","dependents":[],"dependson":[{"id":"ai-terminal-j38","content_hash":"6b3bcb1f4cd3d99fd6db3d60d383187d4f547e6ea26855dccc31ada6e1df76fb","dependency_type":"discovered-from"}]}
